Title: The Lighthouse
Author: The VoxDown authors
Notes: A fresh screenplay for trying `vxd import`. Free to copy (CC0).

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

Rain on the windows. A lamp turns slowly overhead. [[Keep the lamp's hum under everything.]]

MARGARET, seventy and unbothered, winds the clock. TOM, ten, watches from the stairs.

TOM
(whispering)
Grandma? Is the storm going to knock us over?

MARGARET
This lighthouse has stood for a hundred years.
(beat)
It is not about to fall over for a bit of weather.

TOM
How do you know?

MARGARET (CONT'D)
Because I asked it. Go to bed.

===

EXT. ROCKS - DAWN

The sea is flat and silver. A small boat rounds the point.

TOM (V.O.)
She was right. She was always right.

CUT TO:

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - MORNING

MARGARET
Breakfast!
